  "scientific_conclusion": "With all physical parameters, the projected Shakhov collision model and the 32x96 mapped-polar velocity rule frozen, refinement from 8x8 to 12x12 to 16x16 monotonically reduced the average heat-flux error from 23.8317% to 16.6215% to 13.0630% and reduced wall-velocity relative RMS from 4.3420 to 2.8660 to 2.0835. The sequence is improving but not spatially converged: the 12x12-to-16x16 profile change remains too large for a cross-Knudsen claim. A linear-in-h extrapolation gives qav=0.0736375 (2.2743% from the literature value) and wall-velocity RMS 0.4455, but this extrapolation is diagnostic rather than validation. No physical or velocity-quadrature parameter was retuned."
